---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteContent, type Locale } from '../../data/siteContent';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [];
}

const { article } = Astro.props;
const locale: Locale = 'en';
const content = siteContent[locale];
---

<BaseLayout title={`${article.title} | ${content.name}`} description={article.excerpt} locale={locale}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <p class="section-label">{article.category}</p>
    <h1 class="section-title mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">{article.title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-muted)]">{article.readTime}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
      <p>Good architecture is not only about the flow of data or the structure of services. It is about how teams reason about the system, make trade-offs explicit and keep moving without creating hidden complexity.</p>
      <p>When engineering teams are growing, the essential question is not whether the system can scale in theory; it is whether the organization can keep it understandable in practice. That means small design decisions, clear responsibilities and an honest view of what is worth optimizing.</p>
      <p>Strong technical leadership makes those trade-offs visible. It creates room for debate, reduces avoidable rework and keeps the architecture aligned with the real needs of the business.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
